Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns, usage and typical conditions in this task  
• `bigquery-public-data.iowa_liquor_sales.sales`  
  - `date`: filter to 2022 (`WHERE date BETWEEN '2022-01-01' AND '2022-12-31'`)  
  - `county`: filter to Dubuque County (`WHERE UPPER(county) = 'DUBUQUE'`)  
  - `category_name`: isolate Bourbon Whiskey rows (e.g. `WHERE LOWER(category_name) LIKE '%bourbon%whiskey%'`)  
  - `sale_dollars`: measure of sales; aggregate for totals / per–capita calculations  
  - `zip_code`: identify ZIP code of the store; after cleaning (e.g. `SUBSTR(zip_code,1,5)`)

• `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_usa.population_by_zip_2010`  
  - `zipcode`: join key to liquor‐sales ZIP  
  - `minimum_age` / `maximum_age`: select rows whose age‑range covers ages 21+  
  - `population`: aggregate to get 21‑and‑over population for each ZIP (`SUM(population)`)  
  - `gender`: pick overall totals (`gender IS NULL OR gender = ''`)

Typical conditions for population table  
```
WHERE (gender IS NULL OR gender = '')
  AND (
        minimum_age >= 21                                   -- age‑range starts at 21 or more
        OR (minimum_age IS NULL AND maximum_age IS NULL)    -- entire pop (if needed)
        OR (minimum_age <= 21 AND (maximum_age IS NULL OR maximum_age >= 21))
      )
```


